redjen@gmail.com writes:
> I play QT Nethack on MacOS X. Whenever I walk over a pile of 2-4 items,
> a new window pops up that lists those items, which I then need to
> dismiss. I find it annoying, especially when walking over multiple
> piles of items, and would like to suppress it. When I walk over a pile
> of 5+ items, I just see a message that "There are several items here."
> I would like that to happen when I walk over a pile of 2-4 items.
> 
> I've searched the archive and looked over the options section of the
> guidebook,  but I can't find any information on how to do this.
> Hopefully, I'm just missing it. Is there a way of changing this
> behavior by altering .nethackrc. 

No. It's hardcoded behaviour, so you'd need to alter the code (the
look_here() function).

--- nethack-3.4.3/src/invent.c  Wed Mar 30 10:11:18 2005
+++ nethack-3.4.3bis/src/invent.c       Tue Oct 11 19:46:52 2005
@@ -2160,7 +2160,7 @@
        const char *dfeature = (char *)0;
        char fbuf[BUFSZ], fbuf2[BUFSZ];
        winid tmpwin;
-       boolean skip_objects = (obj_cnt >= 5), felt_cockatrice = FALSE;
+       boolean skip_objects = (obj_cnt >= 2), felt_cockatrice = FALSE;

